{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CggzTURMte5ehJiMr5Yah","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Method.** I used the standard strong-field (low-spin) d⁶ expressions, with ¹A₁g as the ground state. I wrote them from memory rather than deriving them from the full Tanabe–Sugano matrices, so they are a second-order approximation.\n\n- E(¹T₁g) = Δ − C + 86B²/Δ\n- E(¹T₂g) = Δ + 16B − C + 90B²/Δ\n\nHere Δ = 10Dq, and I set C = 4.5B.\n\n**Solving.**\n\n1. Subtracting the two expressions gives E(¹T₂g) − E(¹T₁g) = 16B + 4B²/Δ. The observed difference is 23 529 − 16 611 = 6918 cm⁻¹.\n2. Solving 16B + 4B²/Δ = 6918 iteratively, with Δ taken from the ¹T₁g equation, gives B ≈ 430 cm⁻¹.\n3. Then C = 4.5B ≈ 1934 cm⁻¹.\n4. Putting this into the ¹T₁g equation gives 16 611 + 4.5(429.8) ≈ 18 545 = Δ + 86B²/Δ. Solving for Δ gives Δ ≈ 17 645 cm⁻¹, so Dq ≈ 1764 cm⁻¹.\n\n**Result:** Dq ≈ 1.76 × 10³ cm⁻¹ (10Dq ≈ 17 650 cm⁻¹), B ≈ 430 cm⁻¹, and C ≈ 1934 cm⁻¹ (fixed by C/B = 4.5).\n\n{\"Dq\": 1764, \"B\": 430, \"C\": 1934, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Low-spin d6 Tanabe-Sugano strong-field expressions for 1T1g and 1T2g solved with C/B=4.5.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1673,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1673,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8e7e548-a444-4536-af20-63e9b368567b","uuid":"a063e2b7-4ea9-4eb9-98c1-e91ac833bc70","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:06:49.993Z","request_id":"req_011CggzTU4Y5zzCixphjoi3Q"}
